    motivation: "A useful scaling theory should explain both when extrapolation works and when practical optimization departs from the idealized dynamics.",
    resolution: "A finite-compute approximation theorem with explicit error terms and valid parameter regimes, or a controlled counterexample showing which condition is indispensable. Reproducing a fitted sigmoid is not sufficient.",
    gap: "Cheng et al. already derive approximation results in a frozen-feature gradient-flow model; ScaleRL establishes empirical predictability in measured recipes. The extension concerns finite-batch practical dynamics and identifiable failure regimes.",
