    statement: "Study horizon-H finite MDPs on common state/action sets whose transition kernels are mixtures of r unknown shared kernels. A world draws a mixture vector; each structure perturbs it within total-variation radius eta; tasks draw bounded linear rewards from a k-dimensional shared basis. Under fixed world/structure/task sampling laws and coverage constants, derive matching new-world policy-risk bounds in the numbers of worlds, structures, tasks and trajectories, and optimize their allocation at explicit acquisition costs.",
    assumptions: ["Define latent dimension/rank, world and task sampling laws, horizon and coverage. Distinguish training generalization to a new world from a new task in an observed world.", "Do not impose empirical exponent values or their ordering as axioms. Include identifiable classes where the allocation ordering differs.", "Account for dependent trajectories and the sparse pattern of observed task-environment pairs; a full Cartesian product is a separate assumption."],
