    statement: "Model binary step judges as conditionally independent given a latent error mode with r possible values; the unknown mode distribution depends on the task, so a mode can make all judges share a systematic mistake. On finite horizon-H task trees, learn a costed combination of additional judges, critique and trusted labels. Bound aggregate error and downstream policy reward after fitting a process verifier, with explicit dependence on latent-mode identifiability and policy-shift coverage.",
    assumptions: ["Specify a dependence model for judge errors conditional on task difficulty and a way to estimate its parameters; do not assume independent errors solely because random seeds differ.", "Keep aggregation, sequential critique and label selection explicit. Include the possibility that a confident majority shares one systematic error.", "Separate static label risk from policy-induced distribution shift and bound each under stated coverage assumptions."],
