    statement: "Use horizon-H state-composition tasks on a finite S-state map alphabet, with reward only for the correct final state, and a two-layer ReLU policy whose hidden features and softmax output weights are both trained. Starting from Gaussian initialization and minibatch REINFORCE, derive a finite-width approximation valid over a growing training horizon. Quantify when learned features improve held-out map-sequence success over training only the output weights, charging both algorithms the same rollout and update budget.",
