    statement: "Let tasks be depth-H expression trees generated by a finite grammar of K operations on S latent states, with observable terminal inputs and answers but unlabelled intermediate states. A shared finite-width neural policy learns both state embeddings and composition from binary final-answer reward. Characterize which grammar reachability, task-coverage and initial-success conditions permit learning unseen compositions in polynomial samples and computation, and give a hardness regime within the same grammar class.",
