    statement: "For binary prediction on a finite context/action space, fix G observable subgroups, all contiguous windows of length at least W, a total-variation drift budget V and a minimum logging propensity p_min. Labels are revealed only by paid audits or a specified selection rule. Determine the attainable answer-rate and audit-cost trade-off for simultaneously bounding selective error in every sufficiently sampled subgroup/window with probability 1-delta, including adaptive actions that change future observations.",
    assumptions: ["Define the loss, abstention action, subgroup complexity, minimum group mass and time-window lengths; arbitrary exact individual-conditional coverage is excluded by known impossibility results.", "Specify when labels arrive, which propensities are known or estimated, and how decisions affect logging. Unobserved outcomes require an access or identification assumption.", "Require an answering-rate or set-size comparison to avoid a vacuous always-abstain or all-labels solution; bound query cost and deployment horizon explicitly."],
